                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "99d7f331-cd67-3bd5-b8eb-dd10c0686a36",
                        "entry_id": "f1ef1243-3d7b-3e72-90c5-ce197da24451",
                        "glosses": [
                            "мифол. в древнегреческой мифологии — бог неба, грома и молний, главный из богов-олимпийцев, сын титана Кроноса и Реи"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1960780-1a75-43f3-8d59-a231913eed5d",
                                "sense_id": "99d7f331-cd67-3bd5-b8eb-dd10c0686a36",
                                "text": "Про главного бога Зевса учили, что он был силен и страшен; кто ему угождал, тому он давал во всем удачу, а на кого гневался, на того пускал молнию и убивал."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4e3dd2fb-760c-42a9-a063-204094827405",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1ef1243-3d7b-3e72-90c5-ce197da24451",
                        "source_sense_id": "99d7f331-cd67-3bd5-b8eb-dd10c0686a36",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zeus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zeus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a56010b-c49c-3cc4-b055-a91735a961cb",
                                        "entry_id": "5e3bd964-ca5a-3cb6-9970-b0081f3cf175",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Supreme ruler of all Greek gods, husband to Hera."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c572c7ab-0c18-3ddf-ac17-03e154bb96e7",
                                        "entry_id": "5e3bd964-ca5a-3cb6-9970-b0081f3cf175",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e05b202a-b0ca-3bf4-8c69-6c14089c277b",
                                        "entry_id": "5e3bd964-ca5a-3cb6-9970-b0081f3cf175",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A representative given name for a dog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60290371-4fec-40e8-9264-fb01126fe529",
                                                "sense_id": "e05b202a-b0ca-3bf4-8c69-6c14089c277b",
                                                "text": "67 give zeus a bath Wash off whatever your dog rolled in over the weekend. It'll freshen up your house and you'll burn about 100 calories."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ceffed7b-8cc1-4956-b239-5298541113f7",
                                                "sense_id": "e05b202a-b0ca-3bf4-8c69-6c14089c277b",
                                                "text": "Eventually, he was named the world’s tallest male dog, taking over the title from fellow Great Dane Zeus who also died aged three in September, after suffering from bone cancer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4ad7260-5a1e-4d92-bda4-b7922034c734",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1ef1243-3d7b-3e72-90c5-ce197da24451",
                        "source_sense_id": "99d7f331-cd67-3bd5-b8eb-dd10c0686a36",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zeus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zeus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1f8540b-a7f0-3b80-9f7b-048351e97bb6",
                                        "entry_id": "a7cffe72-0bb7-3c1e-8711-7a2f2de9a501",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "höchster der olympischen Götter, Himmels- und Wettergott. Gatte der Hera."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "(antike) griechische"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8955474d-0d05-495b-afe4-61333f6c3be1",
                                                "sense_id": "c1f8540b-a7f0-3b80-9f7b-048351e97bb6",
                                                "text": "Die wohl bekannteste Darstellung des Zeus ist die heute nicht mehr erhaltene Kolossalstatue des Phidias in Olympia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2c2454b-d0c0-41bc-81d3-2536b419ed94",
                                                "sense_id": "c1f8540b-a7f0-3b80-9f7b-048351e97bb6",
                                                "text": "„Spätestens seit dem 7. Jahrhundert war Olympia ein Heiligtum des Zeus.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d485ae1a-c6a1-416f-a46d-a2278ced1781",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1ef1243-3d7b-3e72-90c5-ce197da24451",
                        "source_sense_id": "99d7f331-cd67-3bd5-b8eb-dd10c0686a36",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zeus",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zeus",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bb24707-c825-301b-8f95-3a05ef75c309",
                                        "entry_id": "4eb5e94e-3a95-34a0-803d-3170236dfa50",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dieu du ciel et de l’orage, roi des dieux et des humains, dont les symboles sont l’aigle et le foudre, dernier fils de Cronos et de Rhéa."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Divinité"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fb60f7a-84ab-466b-8549-78800b49705d",
                                                "sense_id": "6bb24707-c825-301b-8f95-3a05ef75c309",
                                                "text": "Invisible et sans rien troubler de ma présence, comme un Zeus vêtu d’air aux âges d’innocence, que ne puis-je « inspecter » le grand travail des champs!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0803db2-5e39-4a51-b0e6-caf80f761559",
                                                "sense_id": "6bb24707-c825-301b-8f95-3a05ef75c309",
                                                "text": "En sixième, quand on a fait la mythologie grecque, je me suis dit que c’était normal que les gouers, ils croyaient que Jésus était le fils de Dieu parce que leurs ancêtres, ils croyaient bien qu’Héraclès était le fils de Zeus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ebcae0c-6f10-4c75-b1f6-d25a92691062",
                                                "sense_id": "6bb24707-c825-301b-8f95-3a05ef75c309",
                                                "text": "Un dieu brillant, éclatant, qui a le soleil pour œil, ne peut être que le dieu-ciel, ou le dieu-soleil, soit un Zeus, un Varuṇa, soit un Indra, un Odin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
